  "result": "Reservations with expiry are now in `src/store.js` and `src/api.js`, and `npm test` passes (173 tests, 0 failed). The new tests are in `test/reservations.test.js`.\n\n- **Store:** I added `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable`. `removeItem` now checks against available stock rather than physical stock. All timing uses the store's `clock`, and a reservation counts as expired once `clock() >= creation time + ttlMs`.\n- **API:**\n  - `GET /stock/:sku` now returns `available`.\n  - The three reservation endpoints return the statuses you specified.\n  - Any error from `POST /reservations` other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` (409) returns 400 with its message.\n- **Tests:** they cover your six store points, including expiry at exactly the TTL boundary, and the API flow with its status codes.\n\n- **Return value:** `confirm(id)` returns `{ sku, stock }` so the API can build its response.\n- **No ttlMs check:** `reserve` doesn't validate `ttlMs`, since you didn't specify what counts as valid. A missing or non-numeric value gives a reservation that never counts as active, so it won't hold any stock.\n- **Expired entries kept:** expired reservations stay in memory. That way `confirm` can return `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`.",
